Here is the **supported text** from the primary Umbrian Assembly press release, and the clean distinction between the **regional vote** and any wider legal effect. ([consiglio.regione.umbria.it](https://consiglio.regione.umbria.it/informazione/notizie/comunicati/assistenza-sanitaria-alla-morte-volontaria-medicalmente-assistita))

### What the press release actually says
The release says the regional assembly approved, by majority on **22 October 2026 at 19:27**, a popular initiative bill titled **“Disposizioni per l’assistenza sanitaria regionale alla morte volontaria medicalmente assistita mediante autosomministrazione di farmaco letale.”** It reports the vote as **11 yes, 3 abstentions, 6 no**, and notes that the president did not vote. ([consiglio.regione.umbria.it](https://consiglio.regione.umbria.it/informazione/notizie/comunicati/assistenza-sanitaria-alla-morte-volontaria-medicalmente-assistita))

### The Pernazza amendments: supported wording
The relevant paragraph says the text was modified by amendments signed by **Laura Pernazza (FI)** on these points:  
- **verification of access conditions** to medically assisted voluntary death **“sulla base della disciplina statale e alla giurisprudenza costituzionale”**;  
- **guaranteeing access to palliative care** without delaying the procedure;  
- the **collegial form** of the commission’s opinion;  
- checking that the patient was informed about palliative care;  
- the **possibility for the person to suspend or revoke their request**;  
- insertion of a **“clausola valutativa”**. ([consiglio.regione.umbria.it](https://consiglio.regione.umbria.it/informazione/notizie/comunicati/assistenza-sanitaria-alla-morte-volontaria-medicalmente-assistita))

### What this means legally
The release describes a **regional legislative vote in Umbria**. It does **not** say that Italy as a whole changed its law, and it does **not** itself announce a nationwide reform. The phrase about access conditions being checked under **state law and constitutional jurisprudence** is a **limit inside the regional text**, not a claim that the region can override national law or the Constitutional Court. ([consiglio.regione.umbria.it](https://consiglio.regione.umbria.it/informazione/notizie/comunicati/assistenza-sanitaria-alla-morte-volontaria-medicalmente-assistita))

### Genuine contradiction?
From the press release itself, I do **not** see a genuine contradiction. The text is internally consistent: it says the Assembly approved a **regional** bill, and that one amendment requires consistency with **state law and constitutional case law**. That is a legal constraint, not a conflict. ([consiglio.regione.umbria.it](https://consiglio.regione.umbria.it/informazione/notizie/comunicati/assistenza-sanitaria-alla-morte-volontaria-medicalmente-assistita))

